# sample.conllu — Turkish temporal corpus sample
# Each sentence = one time-slice; # date = YYYY-MM-DD
# HEAD/DEPREL (columns 7/8) were added by hand to demonstrate
# collocation_mode=syntactic: each recognizable compound noun phrase
# (e.g. "yapay zeka") is chained head-finally with amod/compound, and
# each phrase's own head gets HEAD=0/root. Several independent phrases
# share one line (this corpus is a keyword list per date, not real
# running text), so a line can have more than one root -- this is a
# simplified, manually-annotated demo, not a treebank-quality parse.

